VTE (GTK4 build): convert touchpad scroll deltas to wheel units before counting clicks

GTK4 delivers touchpad scrolling in surface units (logical pixels of finger travel), wheel
scrolling in wheel units (one per notch). VTE's GTK4 widget passes the deltas through
unchanged, so every pixel of two-finger travel becomes one wheel click for programs that
capture the mouse (less, vim, htop, Claude Code's fullscreen UI) and ceil(rows/10) fake
arrow keys on the alternate screen: the smallest motion scrolls a screenful. The GTK3 build
got deltas pre-divided by GTK. Divide surface-unit deltas by the cell size, so one wheel
unit is one text line of finger travel, which is what the GTK3 build and other terminals do.

Upstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/vte/-/issues/2720 (open), patch by samar on that
issue (2026-10-29), applies unchanged to vte 0.84.1. Drop this file once VTE fixes it.

--- a/src/widget.cc
+++ b/src/widget.cc
@@ -1322,6 +1322,15 @@ Widget::event_scroll(GtkEventControllerScroll* controller,
 {
         _vte_debug_print(vte::debug::category::EVENTS, "Scroll delta_x={:.3f} delta_y={:.3f}", dx, dy);
 
+        if (gtk_event_controller_scroll_get_unit(controller) == GDK_SCROLL_UNIT_SURFACE) {
+                auto const cell_width = terminal()->get_cell_width();
+                auto const cell_height = terminal()->get_cell_height();
+                if (cell_width > 0)
+                        dx /= cell_width;
+                if (cell_height > 0)
+                        dy /= cell_height;
+        }
+
         auto event = gtk_event_controller_get_current_event(GTK_EVENT_CONTROLLER(controller));
         if (!event)
                 return false;
